{
  "experiment": "Pool the identical class-stratified subsamples from all five folds into a single inference batch. Every row is unique, all class heads and style evidence were prompt-held-out, and both selectors use scores only. The only Qwen input is the public CHEN single-passage OOF head, not the 45-input leaderboard ensemble. Selectors operate across predictions from different fitted folds. Other-fold predictions can depend on this fold during their training, so this is a runtime-scale component stress test, not an independent leaderboard estimate. The prior is the prespecified uniform law over 18 labels. No validation class frequencies are fitted or used at inference. Sample membership uses the same frozen simulations as marginal-shift-controls.json. The 12-source simulation is exploratory and can give a handful of texts substantial weight under balanced accuracy.",
